[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Mad or Not?]
[00:14.26]Why do people think the writer is mad?
[00:20.48]Aeroplanes are slowly driving me mad.
[00:25.75]I live near an airport and passing planes can be heard night and day.
[00:33.99]The airport was built years ago,
[00:38.36]but for some reason it could not be used then.
[00:43.76]Last year, however, it came into use.
[00:48.69]Over a hundred people must have been driven away from their homes by the noise.
[00:55.18]I am one of the few people left.
[00:59.25]Sometimes I think this house will be knocked down by a passing plane.
[01:06.18]I have been offered a large sum of money to go away,
[01:11.64]but I am determined to stay here.
[01:15.13]Everybody says I must be mad and they are probably right.
